--TEST--
`Core\Response::addCookie` takes every option its call site left out from `[http.cookies]`, and the defaults are observable through the two rules that read them -- `rule:http-server/cookies-are-secure-httponly-and-lax`, spec § 15
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Response\SameSite
// Invariance over a sweep, and the sweep is the options bag. Nothing here reads
// a header back — that crossing is asserted in `nvs-server`, where a response
// exists — so what pins the defaults is that two *rules* read them, and each
// rule answers differently depending on what the unwritten option was.

// § 3's pair: `SameSite=None` needs `Secure`. Written alone it is admitted,
// and that is only true if `secure` defaulted to `true` — with nothing
// configured, `rule:http-server/cookies-are-secure-httponly-and-lax` says it does.
uint $admitted = 0;
try {
    Core\Response::addCookie("sid", "abc", {sameSite: Core\Response\SameSite::None});
    $admitted = $admitted + 1;
} catch (LogicError $dropped) {
}
echo "SameSite::None alone was admitted ", $admitted, " time\n";

// Write the other half of the pair and the same cookie is refused, by the same
// rule the boot refusal uses on the same two keys.
uint $pair = 0;
try {
    Core\Response::addCookie("sid", "abc", {sameSite: Core\Response\SameSite::None, secure: false});
} catch (LogicError $meaningless) {
    $pair = $pair + 1;
}
echo "SameSite::None without Secure was refused ", $pair, " of 1\n";

// The pair is `None`'s alone: the other two cases are an ordinary cookie
// without `Secure`, so a member that had refused on `secure: false` generally
// would fail here while still looking right on the line above.
array<Core\Response\SameSite> $cases = [
    Core\Response\SameSite::Lax,
    Core\Response\SameSite::Strict,
];
uint $insecure = 0;
foreach ($cases as Core\Response\SameSite $case) {
    try {
        Core\Response::addCookie("sid", "abc", {sameSite: $case, secure: false});
        $insecure = $insecure + 1;
    } catch (LogicError $unexpected) {
    }
}
echo "Lax and Strict without Secure were admitted ", $insecure, " of 2\n";

// The second rule that reads a default is `rule:errors/cookie-name-bytes`'s `__Host-`, which
// requires `Path=/`. A bare call conforms, so the unwritten `path` was `/`;
// writing any other path breaks it. This is the `path` default asserted
// through a rule rather than read off a line.
uint $rooted = 0;
try {
    Core\Response::addCookie("__Host-a", "abc");
    $rooted = $rooted + 1;
} catch (LogicError $elsewhere) {
}
try {
    Core\Response::addCookie("__Host-b", "abc", {path: "/"});
    $rooted = $rooted + 1;
} catch (LogicError $spelled) {
}
echo "the unwritten path and `/` agree, ", $rooted, " of 2\n";

// A path is an attribute and carries what an attribute can: never empty, and
// never a semicolon, which would begin one the program did not write.
array<string> $paths = ["", "/a;Domain=evil.test"];
uint $refusedPaths = 0;
foreach ($paths as string $bad) {
    try {
        Core\Response::addCookie("sid", "abc", {path: $bad});
    } catch (LogicError $unattributable) {
        $refusedPaths = $refusedPaths + 1;
    }
}
echo "refused ", $refusedPaths, " of 2 paths\n";

// `maxAge` is the one option `[http.cookies]` deliberately does not configure:
// unwritten is a session cookie, and every non-negative duration is a lifetime.
// A sub-second one truncates to `Max-Age=0`, which is the deletion `0s` spells
// and the honest reading of a cookie that expires before it arrives.
array<Core\Time\Duration> $ages = [0s, 20ms, 2s];
uint $aged = 0;
foreach ($ages as Core\Time\Duration $age) {
    try {
        Core\Response::addCookie("sid", "abc", {maxAge: $age});
        $aged = $aged + 1;
    } catch (LogicError $unlivable) {
    }
}
echo "took ", $aged, " of 3 lifetimes\n";

// And the whole bag left out is the shipped policy, written in one call and
// with no byte of body.
var $quiet = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    Core\Response::addCookie("sid", "abc");
});
echo "a defaulted cookie wrote [", $quiet, "]\n";
--EXPECT--
SameSite::None alone was admitted 1 time
SameSite::None without Secure was refused 1 of 1
Lax and Strict without Secure were admitted 2 of 2
the unwritten path and `/` agree, 2 of 2
refused 2 of 2 paths
took 3 of 3 lifetimes
a defaulted cookie wrote []
